\s1 Xerxes’ Royal Feast
\p \v 1 \rb This is what happened|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֑וֹשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Ahasuerus\ft ; here and throughout Esther \f*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb*\rb |אֲחַשְׁוֵר֗וֹשׁ\rb* \rb who reigned over|הַמֹּלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb 127|שֶׁ֛בַע\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינָֽה׃\rb* \rb from India|מֵהֹ֣דּוּ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Cush|כּ֔וּשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 1:1 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \v 2 \rb In those|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֗וֹשׁ\rb* \rb sat|כְּשֶׁ֣בֶת׀\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb his royal|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָֽה׃\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֥ן\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb In the third|שָׁלוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb Xerxes held|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials|שָׂרָ֖יו\rb* \rb and servants|וַעֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*. \rb The military leaders|חֵ֣יל׀\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֣ס\rb* \rb and Media|וּמָדַ֗י\rb* \rb were there|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*, \rb along with the nobles|הַֽפַּרְתְּמִ֛ים\rb* \rb and princes|וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the provinces|הַמְּדִינ֖וֹת\rb*. \v 4 \rb And for a full|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb 180|שְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמְאַ֖ת\rb*\rb |יֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb he displayed|בְּהַרְאֹת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the glorious|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֙שֶׁר֙\rb* \rb of his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb the magnificent|תִּפְאֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb splendor|יְקָ֔ר\rb* \rb of his greatness|גְּדוּלָּת֑וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb At the end|וּבִמְל֣וֹאת׀\rb* \rb of this|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִ֣ים\rb*, \rb in the garden|גִּנַּ֥ת\rb* \rb court|בַּחֲצַ֕ר\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace|בִּיתַ֖ן\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb held|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a seven-day|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |הַנִּמְצְאִים֩\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָ֜ה\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֨ן\rb*, \rb from the least|קָטָ֛ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the greatest|לְמִגָּ֧דוֹל\rb*. \v 6 \rb Hangings of white|ח֣וּר׀\rb* \rb and blue|וּתְכֵ֗לֶת\rb* \rb linen|כַּרְפַּ֣ס\rb* \rb were fastened|אָחוּז֙\rb* \rb with cords|בְּחַבְלֵי־\rb* \rb of fine white|ב֣וּץ\rb* \rb and purple material|וְאַרְגָּמָ֔ן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb silver|כֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb rings|גְּלִ֥ילֵי\rb* \rb on the marble|שֵׁ֑שׁ\rb* \rb pillars|וְעַמּ֣וּדֵי\rb*. \rb Gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכֶ֗סֶף\rb* \rb couches|מִטּ֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb were arranged|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb on a mosaic pavement|רִֽצְפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of porphyry|בַּהַט־\rb*, \rb marble|וָשֵׁ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb mother-of-pearl|וְדַ֥ר\rb*, \rb and other costly stones|וְסֹחָֽרֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Beverages were served|וְהַשְׁקוֹת֙\rb* \rb in an array of goblets|בִּכְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*, \rb each|וְכֵלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מִכֵּלִ֣ים\rb* \rb with a different design|שׁוֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the royal|מַלְכ֛וּת\rb* \rb wine|וְיֵ֥ין\rb* \rb flowed freely|רָ֖ב\rb*, \rb according to the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb bounty|כְּיַ֥ד\rb*. \v 8 \rb By|כַדָּ֖ת\rb* \rb order|יִסַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, \rb no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb limit was placed|אֹנֵ֑ס\rb* \rb on the drinking|וְהַשְּׁתִיָּ֥ה\rb*,\rb |עַ֚ל\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb official|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb of his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb was to serve|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb each|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb man|וָאִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb whatever he desired|כִּרְצ֥וֹן\rb*.
\s1 Queen Vashti’s Refusal
\p \v 9 \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֣י\rb* \rb also|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb gave|עָשְׂתָ֖ה\rb* \rb a banquet|מִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb for the women|נָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb in the royal|הַמַּלְכ֔וּת\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֚ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb of King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֽוֹשׁ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb*, \rb when the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb was merry|כְּט֥וֹב\rb* \rb with wine|בַּיָּ֑יִן\rb*, \rb he ordered|אָמַ֡ר\rb* \rb the seven|שִׁבְעַת֙\rb* \rb eunuchs|הַסָּ֣רִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb who served|הַמְשָׁ֣רְתִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb him|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* — \rb Mehuman|לִ֠מְהוּמָן\rb*, \rb Biztha|בִּזְּתָ֨א\rb*, \rb Harbona|חַרְבוֹנָ֜א\rb*, \rb Bigtha|בִּגְתָ֤א\rb*, \rb Abagtha|וַאֲבַגְתָא֙\rb*, \rb Zethar|זֵתַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and Carkas|וְכַרְכַּ֔ס\rb* — \v 11 \rb to bring|לְ֠הָבִיא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֛ה\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֧י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb wearing her royal|מַלְכ֑וּת\rb* \rb crown|בְּכֶ֣תֶר\rb*, \rb to display|לְהַרְא֨וֹת\rb* \rb her beauty|יָפְיָ֔הּ\rb* \rb to the people|הָֽעַמִּ֤ים\rb* \rb and officials|וְהַשָּׂרִים֙\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she was|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb beautiful|טוֹבַ֥ת\rb* \rb to behold|מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb Vashti, however|וַשְׁתִּ֗י\rb*, \rb refused|וַתְּמָאֵ֞ן\rb* \rb to come|לָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb brought by|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb his eunuchs|הַסָּרִיסִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb became furious|וַיִּקְצֹ֤ף\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb*, \rb and his anger|וַחֲמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb burned|בָּעֲרָ֥ה\rb* \rb within him|בֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Queen Vashti Deposed
\p \v 13 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb consulted|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the wise men|לַחֲכָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb who knew|יֹדְעֵ֣י\rb* \rb the times|הָֽעִתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb for it was|כִּי־\rb* \rb customary|כֵן֙\rb* \rb for him|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to confer|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb with|לִפְנֵ֕י\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the experts|יֹדְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb in law|דָּ֥ת\rb* \rb and justice|וָדִֽין׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb His closest advisors were|וְהַקָּרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb Carshena|כַּרְשְׁנָ֤א\rb*, \rb Shethar|שֵׁתָר֙\rb*, \rb Admatha|אַדְמָ֣תָא\rb*, \rb Tarshish|תַרְשִׁ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb Meres|מֶ֥רֶס\rb*, \rb Marsena|מַרְסְנָ֖א\rb*, \rb and Memucan|מְמוּכָ֑ן\rb*, \rb the seven|שִׁבְעַ֞ת\rb* \rb princes|שָׂרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֣ס\rb* \rb and Media|וּמָדַ֗י\rb* \rb who had personal access to|רֹאֵי֙\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and ranked|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb highest|רִאשֹׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the kingdom|בַּמַּלְכֽוּת׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 “\rb According to law|כְּדָת֙\rb*,” \rb he asked, “what|מַֽה־\rb* \rb should be done|לַּעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb with Queen|בַּמַּלְכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֑י\rb*, \rb since|עַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she refused to obey|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |עָשְׂתָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the command|מַאֲמַר֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb delivered by|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb the eunuchs|הַסָּרִיסִֽים׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 16 \rb And in the presence|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and his princes|וְהַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb Memucan|מוּמְכָן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֣י\rb* \rb has wronged|עָוְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the princes|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the provinces|מְדִינ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the conduct|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the queen|הַמַּלְכָּה֙\rb* \rb will become known|יֵצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb women|הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb causing them to despise|לְהַבְז֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵיהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb their husbands|בַּעְלֵיהֶ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 1:17 \ft Or \fqa to disdain their husbands in their eyes\f* \rb and say|בְּאָמְרָ֗ם\rb*, ‘\rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֡וֹשׁ\rb* \rb ordered|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֛ה\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֧י\rb* \rb to be brought|לְהָבִ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb*, \rb but she did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb come|בָֽאָה׃\rb*.’
\p \v 18 \rb This|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb very day|וְֽהַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb the noble women|שָׂר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּֽרַס־\rb* \rb and Media|וּמָדַ֗י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb have heard|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb about|אֶת־\rb* \rb the queen’s|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb conduct|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb will say|תֹּאמַ֣רְנָה׀\rb* \rb the same thing to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb*, \rb resulting in much|וּכְדַ֖י\rb* \rb contempt|בִּזָּי֥וֹן\rb* \rb and wrath|וָקָֽצֶף׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb So if|אִם־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֗וֹב\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מִלְּפָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb let him issue|יֵצֵ֤א\rb* \rb a royal|מַלְכוּת֙\rb* \rb decree|דְבַר־\rb*, \rb and let it be recorded|וְיִכָּתֵ֛ב\rb* \rb in the laws|בְּדָתֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Persia|פָֽרַס־\rb* \rb and Media|וּמָדַ֖י\rb* \rb so that it cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be repealed|יַעֲב֑וֹר\rb*, \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֗י\rb* \rb shall never again|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb enter|תָב֜וֹא\rb* \rb the presence|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb and that her royal position|וּמַלְכוּתָהּ֙\rb* \rb shall be given|יִתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to a woman|לִרְעוּתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb better|הַטּוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb than she|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb The edict|פִּתְגָ֨ם\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb issues|יַעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb will be heard|וְנִשְׁמַע֩\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his vast|רַבָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |הִ֑יא\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb* — \rb and so|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb women|הַנָּשִׁ֗ים\rb*, \rb from the least|קָטָֽן׃\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the greatest|לְמִגָּד֖וֹל\rb*, \rb will honor|יִתְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |יְקָר֙\rb* \rb their husbands|לְבַעְלֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his princes|וְהַשָּׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb were pleased|וַיִּיטַב֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb with this counsel|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*; \rb so the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb as Memucan|מְמוּכָֽן׃\rb* \rb advised|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*. \v 22 \rb He sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the provinces|מְדִינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the kingdom|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb each province|מְדִינָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָה֙\rb* \rb in its own script|כִּכְתָבָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb each people|עַ֥ם\rb*\rb |וָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in their own language|כִּלְשׁוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb proclaiming|וּמְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |כִּלְשׁ֥וֹן\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 1:22 \ft Literally \fqa proclaiming in the language of his own people\f* \rb that every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb should be|לִהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb master|שֹׂרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of his own household|בְּבֵית֔וֹ\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Seeking Vashti’s Successor
\p \v 1 \rb Some time later|אַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*,\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb when the anger|חֲמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb had subsided|כְּשֹׁ֕ךְ\rb*, \rb he remembered|זָכַ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּי֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had done|עָשָׂ֔תָה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had been decreed|נִגְזַ֖ר\rb* \rb against her|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb attendants|נַעֲרֵֽי־\rb*\rb |מְשָׁרְתָ֑יו\rb* \rb proposed|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb*, “\rb Let a search be made|יְבַקְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb for beautiful|טוֹב֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb young|נְעָר֥וֹת\rb* \rb virgins|בְּתוּל֖וֹת\rb* \rb for the king|לַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*, \v 3 \rb and let the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb appoint|וְיַפְקֵ֨ד\rb* \rb commissioners|פְּקִידִים֮\rb* \rb in each|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his kingdom|מַלְכוּתוֹ֒\rb* \rb to assemble|וְיִקְבְּצ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the beautiful|טוֹבַ֨ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֜ה\rb* \rb young|נַעֲרָֽה־\rb* \rb women|בְ֠תוּלָה\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the harem|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the citadel|הַבִּירָה֙\rb* \rb of Susa|שׁוּשַׁ֤ן\rb*. \rb Let them be placed|אֶל־\rb* \rb under the care|יַ֥ד\rb* \rb of Hegai|הֵגֶ֛א\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb eunuch|סְרִ֥יס\rb* \rb in charge of|שֹׁמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and let them be given|וְנָת֖וֹן\rb* \rb beauty treatments|תַּמְרוּקֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then let the young woman|וְהַֽנַּעֲרָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb pleases|תִּיטַב֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb become queen|תִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of Vashti|וַשְׁתִּ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb This suggestion|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּיטַ֧ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and he acted|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb accordingly|כֵּֽן׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Esther Finds Favor
\p \v 5 \rb Now there was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the citadel|הַבִּירָ֑ה\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb a Jewish|יְהוּדִ֔י\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb from the tribe of Benjamin|יְמִינִֽי׃\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֗י\rb* \rb son|בֶּ֣ן\rb* \rb of Jair|יָאִ֧יר\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֛י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֖ישׁ\rb*. \v 6 \rb He|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb had been carried into exile|הָגְלָה֙\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלַ֔יִם\rb* \rb by Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb those taken captive|הַגֹּלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הָגְלְתָ֔ה\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Jeconiah|יְכָנְיָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 2:6 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see 2 Kings 24:12.\f* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הֶגְלָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And Mordecai|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb had brought up|אֹמֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hadassah|הֲדַסָּ֗ה\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֤יא\rb*, \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb*), \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of his uncle|דֹּד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb she did not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb have|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb a father|אָ֣ב\rb* \rb or mother|וָאֵ֑ם\rb*. \rb The young woman|וְהַנַּעֲרָ֤ה\rb* \rb was lovely|יְפַת־\rb* \rb in form|תֹּ֙אַר֙\rb* \rb and|וְטוֹבַ֣ת\rb* \rb appearance|מַרְאֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb and when her father|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb had died|וּבְמ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֛י\rb* \rb had taken her|לְקָחָ֧הּ\rb* \rb as his own|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb daughter|לְבַֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb When|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb command|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb and edict|וְדָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb had been proclaimed|בְּהִשָּׁמַ֤ע\rb*, \rb many|רַבּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb young women|נְעָר֥וֹת\rb* \rb gathered|וּֽבְהִקָּבֵ֞ץ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the citadel|הַבִּירָ֖ה\rb* \rb of Susa|שׁוּשַׁ֥ן\rb* \rb under|אֶל־\rb* \rb the care|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Hegai|הֵגָ֑י\rb*. \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb was also taken|וַתִּלָּקַ֤ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and placed under|אֶל־\rb* \rb the care|יַ֥ד\rb* \rb of Hegai|הֵגַ֖י\rb*, \rb the custodian|שֹׁמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of the women|הַנָּשִֽׁים׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And the young woman|הַנַּעֲרָ֣ה\rb* \rb pleased him|וַתִּיטַ֨ב\rb*\rb |בְעֵינָיו֮\rb* \rb and obtained|וַתִּשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb his|לְפָנָיו֒\rb* \rb favor|חֶ֣סֶד\rb*, \rb so he quickly|וַ֠יְבַהֵל\rb* \rb provided|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb her|לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb with beauty treatments|תַּמְרוּקֶ֤יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the special diet|מָנוֹתֶ֙הָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*. \rb He assigned|לָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb to her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb select|הָרְאֻי֥וֹת\rb* \rb maidservants|הַנְּעָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb from the palace|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and transferred her|וַיְשַׁנֶּ֧הָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with them|נַעֲרוֹתֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb to the best|לְט֖וֹב\rb* \rb place|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb in the harem|הַנָּשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb reveal|הִגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb her people|עַמָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb her lineage|מֽוֹלַדְתָּ֑הּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֛י\rb* \rb had instructed|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb her|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to do so|תַגִּֽיד׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And every day|וּבְכָל־\rb*\rb |י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |וָי֔וֹם\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַי֙\rb* \rb would walk back and forth|מִתְהַלֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the court|חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the harem|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb to learn|לָדַ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb about|אֶת־\rb* \rb Esther’s|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb welfare|שְׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb and what|וּמַה־\rb* \rb was happening|יֵּעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to her|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb In the twelve|שְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb months|חֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |יִמְלְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb before her|נַעֲרָ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְנַעֲרָ֜ה\rb* \rb turn|תֹּר֩\rb*\rb |וּבְהַגִּ֡יעַ\rb* \rb to go|לָב֣וֹא׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֗וֹשׁ\rb*,\rb |מִקֵּץ֩\rb*\rb |הֱי֨וֹת\rb* \rb the harem|הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb* \rb regulation required|כְּדָ֤ת\rb* \rb each young woman|הַנָּשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb to receive beauty treatments|מְרוּקֵיהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb with oil|בְּשֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb of myrrh|הַמֹּ֔ר\rb* \rb for six|שִׁשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb and then with perfumes|בַּבְּשָׂמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and cosmetics|וּבְתַמְרוּקֵ֖י\rb* \rb for another six|וְשִׁשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁים֙\rb*. \v 13 \rb When|וּבָזֶ֕ה\rb* \rb the young woman|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb would go|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb she was given|יִנָּ֤תֵֽן\rb* \rb whatever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb she requested|תֹּאמַ֜ר\rb* \rb to take|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb from the harem|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 14 \rb She|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb would go there|בָאָ֗ה\rb* \rb in the evening|בָּעֶ֣רֶב׀\rb*, \rb and in the morning|וּ֠בַבֹּקֶר\rb* \rb she|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb would return|שָׁבָ֞ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb harem|בֵּ֤ית\rb*\rb |הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb*\f + \fr 2:14 \ft Or \fqa to another part of the harem\f* \rb under|אֶל־\rb* \rb the care|יַ֧ד\rb* \rb of Shaashgaz|שַֽׁעֲשְׁגַ֛ז\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb eunuch|סְרִ֥יס\rb* \rb in charge of|שֹׁמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the concubines|הַפִּֽילַגְשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb She would not|לֹא־\rb* \rb return|תָב֥וֹא\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb unless|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb he|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb delighted|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb in her|בָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb and summoned her|וְנִקְרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb by name|בְשֵֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb was the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Abihail|אֲבִיחַ֣יִל\rb*, \rb the uncle|דֹּ֣ד\rb* \rb from whom Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֡י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb had adopted|לָקַֽח־\rb* \rb her|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb as his own daughter|לְבַ֜ת\rb*. \rb And when it was her turn|תֹּר־\rb*\rb |וּבְהַגִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb to go|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, \rb she did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb ask for|בִקְשָׁה֙\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb except|כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |אִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Hegai|הֵגַ֥י\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb trusted official|סְרִיס־\rb* \rb in charge of|שֹׁמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the harem|הַנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\rb |וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb had advised|יֹאמַ֛ר\rb*. \rb And Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb found|נֹשֵׂ֣את\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֔ן\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who saw her|רֹאֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb She|אֶסְתֵּ֜ר\rb* \rb was taken|וַתִּלָּקַ֨ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb in the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֖י\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Tebeth|טֵבֵ֑ת\rb*,\f + \fr 2:16 \fqa Tebeth \ft is the tenth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of December and January.\f* \rb in the seventh|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Esther Becomes Queen
\p \v 17 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֨ב\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb more than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the other women|הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and she found|וַתִּשָּׂא־\rb* \rb grace|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and favor|וָחֶ֛סֶד\rb* \rb in his sight|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb more than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of the other virgins|הַבְּתוּלֹ֑ת\rb*. \rb So he placed|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכוּת֙\rb* \rb crown|כֶּֽתֶר־\rb* \rb upon her head|בְּרֹאשָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb and made her queen|וַיַּמְלִיכֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb Vashti|וַשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb held|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גָד֗וֹל\rb* \rb banquet|מִשְׁתֶּ֣ה\rb*, \rb Esther’s|אֶסְתֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb banquet|מִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials|שָׂרָיו֙\rb* \rb and servants|וַעֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb He proclaimed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb a tax holiday|וַהֲנָחָ֤ה\rb* \rb in the provinces|לַמְּדִינוֹת֙\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb gifts|מַשְׂאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb worthy of the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb bounty|כְּיַ֥ד\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb When the virgins|בְּתוּל֖וֹת\rb* \rb were assembled|וּבְהִקָּבֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֑ית\rb*, \rb Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַֽׁעַר־\rb*.\f + \fr 2:19 \ft Or \fqa Mordecai had become a palace official\f* \v 20 \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֗ר\rb* \rb still had not|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb revealed|מַגֶּ֤דֶת\rb* \rb her lineage|מֽוֹלַדְתָּהּ֙\rb* \rb or her people|עַמָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb had instructed|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb She|אֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb obeyed|עֹשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכַי֙\rb* \rb command|מַאֲמַ֤ר\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb she had done|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb under his care|בְאָמְנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Mordecai Uncovers a Conspiracy
\p \v 21 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*, \rb while Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַֽׁעַר־\rb*, \rb Bigthan|בִּגְתָ֨ן\rb*\f + \fr 2:21 \fqa Bigthan \ft is a variant of \fqa Bigthana\ft ; see Esther 6:2.\f* \rb and Teresh|וָתֶ֜רֶשׁ\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb eunuchs|סָרִיסֵ֤י\rb* \rb who guarded|מִשֹּׁמְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the entrance|הַסַּ֔ף\rb*, \rb grew angry|קָצַף֩\rb* \rb and conspired|וַיְבַקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb to assassinate|לִשְׁלֹ֣חַ\rb*\rb |יָ֔ד\rb* \rb King|בַּמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵֽרֹשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb When Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb learned|וַיִּוָּדַ֤ע\rb* \rb of the plot|הַדָּבָר֙\rb*, \rb he reported|וַיַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb it to Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb*, \rb and she|אֶסְתֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb informed|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb on Mordecai’s behalf|מָרְדֳּכָֽי׃\rb*\rb |בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb After the report|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb had been investigated|וַיְבֻקַּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb and verified|וַיִּמָּצֵ֔א\rb*, \rb both officials|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were hanged|וַיִּתָּל֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|עֵ֑ץ\rb*. \rb And all this was recorded|וַיִּכָּתֵ֗ב\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Or \fqa the Book of the Annals \ft or \fqa the Book of the Historical Events\f* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Haman’s Plot against the Jews
\p \v 1 \rb After|אַחַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb events|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֜וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb honored|גִּדַּל֩\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֧ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Hammedatha|הַמְּדָ֛תָא\rb*, \rb the Agagite|הָאֲגָגִ֖י\rb*, \rb elevating him|וַֽיְנַשְּׂאֵ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֙שֶׂם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to a position|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb above|מֵעַ֕ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the princes|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb bowed down|כֹּרְעִ֤ים\rb* \rb and paid homage|וּמִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִים֙\rb* \rb to Haman|לְהָמָ֔ן\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּה־\rb* \rb that this be done|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb for him|ל֣וֹ\rb*. \rb But Mordecai|וּמָ֨רְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb bow down|יִכְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or pay homage|יִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the royal|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֙וּעַ֙\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb disobey|עוֹבֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb after day|וָי֔וֹם\rb* \rb they warned|בְּאָמְרָם\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb but he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb comply|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So they reported it|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb to Haman|לְהָמָ֗ן\rb* \rb to see|לִרְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb whether Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb behavior|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb would be tolerated|הֲיַֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he had told|הִגִּ֥יד\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was a Jew|יְהוּדִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When Haman|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb would not|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb bow down|כֹּרֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb or pay him homage|וּמִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb he|הָמָ֖ן\rb* \rb was filled|וַיִּמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with rage|חֵמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he learned the identity|הִגִּ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb of Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb* \rb people|עַ֣ם\rb*, \rb he scorned the notion of|וַיִּ֣בֶז\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָ֗יו\rb*\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa he disdained in his eyes\f* \rb laying|לִשְׁלֹ֤ח\rb* \rb hands|יָד֙\rb* \rb on Mordecai|בְּמָרְדֳּכַ֣י\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Instead, he|הָמָ֗ן\rb* \rb sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִ֧יד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכָֽי׃\rb* \rb people|עַ֥ם\rb*, \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֛ים\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֖וֹשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb In the twelfth|שְׁתֵּ֣ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of King|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֑וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb in the first|הָרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Nisan|נִיסָ֔ן\rb*,\f + \fr 3:7 \fqa Nisan \ft is the first month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \rb the Pur|פּוּר֩\rb* \rb (that is|ה֨וּא\rb*, \rb the lot|הַגּוֹרָ֜ל\rb*) \rb was cast|הִפִּ֣יל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֗ן\rb* \rb to determine a day|מִיּ֧וֹם׀\rb*\rb |לְי֛וֹם\rb* \rb and month|וּמֵחֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb*.\rb |לְחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb And the lot fell on the twelfth|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the month of Adar|אֲדָֽר׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 3:7 \ft LXX \fqa was cast before Haman—a day and month—and the lot fell on the fourteenth of the month of Adar\ft ; Hebrew \fqa was cast before Haman a day and month—the twelfth, Adar\ft ; the month of \fqa Adar \ft (also in verse 13) is the twelfth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of February and March.\f*
\p \v 8 \rb Then Haman|הָמָן֙\rb* \rb informed|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*, “\rb There|יֶשְׁנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb is a certain|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb scattered|מְפֻזָּ֤ר\rb* \rb and dispersed|וּמְפֹרָד֙\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb of every|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb province|מְדִינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of your kingdom|מַלְכוּתֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Their laws|וְדָתֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb are different|שֹׁנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb from everyone|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb else’s|עָ֗ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and they do not|אֵינָ֣ם\rb* \rb obey|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb laws|דָּתֵ֤י\rb*. \rb So it is not|אֵין־\rb* \rb in the king’s|וְלַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb best interest|שֹׁוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to tolerate them|לְהַנִּיחָֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb let a decree be issued|יִכָּתֵ֖ב\rb* \rb to destroy them|לְאַבְּדָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I will deposit|לְהָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֨רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֜ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 3:9 \fqa 10,000 talents \ft is approximately 377 tons or 342 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb treasury|גִּנְזֵ֥י\rb* \rb to pay|אֶשְׁקוֹל֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |יְדֵי֙\rb* \rb those who carry it out|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֧סַר\rb* \rb the signet ring|טַבַּעְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb his finger|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb and gave|וַֽיִּתְּנָ֗הּ\rb* \rb it to Haman|לְהָמָ֧ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Hammedatha|הַמְּדָ֛תָא\rb*, \rb the Agagite|הָאֲגָגִ֖י\rb*, \rb the enemy|צֹרֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 11 “\rb Keep your money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to Haman|לְהָמָ֔ן\rb*. “\rb These people|וְהָעָ֕ם\rb* \rb are given|נָת֣וּן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb with them|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb as you please|בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\rb |כַּטּ֥וֹב\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb On the thirteenth|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֮\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb scribes|סֹפְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb were summoned|וַיִּקָּרְאוּ֩\rb* \rb and the order was written|וַיִּכָּתֵ֣ב\rb* \rb exactly as|כְּֽכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֡ן\rb*\rb |אֶ֣ל\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the royal|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶל־\rb* \rb satraps|אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb the governors|הַפַּח֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb of each province|מְדִינָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the officials|שָׂ֤רֵי\rb* \rb of each|עַם֙\rb* \rb people|וָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb in the script|כִּכְתָבָ֔הּ\rb* \rb of each province|וּמְדִינָה֙\rb* \rb and the language|כִּלְשׁוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb of every people|וָעָ֖ם\rb*. \rb It was written|נִכְתָּ֔ב\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb and sealed|וְנֶחְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb with the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb signet ring|בְּטַבַּ֥עַת\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And the letters|סְפָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb were sent|וְנִשְׁל֨וֹחַ\rb* \rb by|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb couriers|הָרָצִים֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb each|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb with the order to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִ֡יד\rb*, \rb kill|לַהֲרֹ֣ג\rb*, \rb and annihilate|וּלְאַבֵּ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַ֠יְּהוּדִים\rb*— \rb young|מִנַּ֨עַר\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֜ן\rb*, \rb women|וְנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and children|טַ֤ף\rb*— \rb and to plunder|לָבֽוֹז׃\rb* \rb their possessions|וּשְׁלָלָ֖ם\rb* \rb on a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*, \rb the thirteenth|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb day of Adar|אֲדָ֑ר\rb*, \rb the twelfth|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb A copy|פַּתְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the text|הַכְּתָ֗ב\rb* \rb of the edict|דָּת֙\rb* \rb was to be issued|לְהִנָּ֤תֵֽן\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb and published|גָּל֖וּי\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָֽעַמִּ֑ים\rb*,\rb |לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb so that they would be ready|עֲתִדִ֖ים\rb* \rb on that|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|לַיּ֥וֹם\rb*. \v 15 \rb The couriers|הָֽרָצִ֞ים\rb* \rb left|יָצְא֤וּ\rb*, \rb spurred on|דְחוּפִים֙\rb* \rb by the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and the edict|וְהַדָּ֥ת\rb* \rb was issued|נִתְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָ֑ה\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb*. \rb Then the king|וְהַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Haman|וְהָמָן֙\rb* \rb sat down|יָשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb but the city|וְהָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Susa|שׁוּשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb was in confusion|נָבֽוֹכָה׃פ\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Mordecai Appeals to Esther
\p \v 1 \rb When Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֗י\rb* \rb learned of|יָדַע֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had happened|נַעֲשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb he|מָרְדֳּכַי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb put on|וַיִּלְבַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂ֖ק\rb* \rb and ashes|וָאֵ֑פֶר\rb*, \rb and went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb into the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb wailing|וַיִּזְעַ֛ק\rb*\rb |זְעָקָ֥ה\rb* \rb loudly|גְדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and bitterly|וּמָרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb But he went only|וַיָּב֕וֹא\rb* \rb as|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb far as the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|שַֽׁעַר־\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the law prohibited|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb anyone wearing|בִּלְב֥וּשׁ\rb* \rb sackcloth|שָֽׂק׃\rb* \rb from entering|לָב֛וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb that|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb In every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֗ה\rb* \rb to which|מְקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb and edict|וְדָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb came|מַגִּ֔יעַ\rb*, \rb there was great|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb mourning|אֵ֤בֶל\rb* \rb among the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb*. \rb They fasted|וְצ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb wept|וּבְכִ֖י\rb*, \rb and lamented|וּמִסְפֵּ֑ד\rb*, \rb and many|לָֽרַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb lay|יֻצַּ֖ע\rb* \rb in sackcloth|שַׂ֣ק\rb* \rb and ashes|וָאֵ֔פֶר\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When Esther’s|אֶסְתֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb maidens|נַעֲר֨וֹת\rb* \rb and eunuchs|וְסָרִיסֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb came|וַ֠תָּבוֹאינָה\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb her about Mordecai|לָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb the queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was overcome with distress|וַתִּתְחַלְחַ֥ל\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*. \rb She sent|וַתִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb clothes|בְּגָדִ֜ים\rb* \rb for Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֗י\rb* \rb to wear|לְהַלְבִּ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb instead of|וּלְהָסִ֥יר\rb* \rb his sackcloth|שַׂקּ֛וֹ\rb*,\rb |מֵעָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb but he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb accept them|קִבֵּֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb summoned|וַתִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb Hathach|לַהֲתָ֜ךְ\rb*, \rb one of the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb eunuchs|מִסָּרִיסֵ֤י\rb* \rb appointed|הֶעֱמִ֣יד\rb* \rb to her|לְפָנֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and she dispatched him|וַתְּצַוֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb* \rb to learn|לָדַ֥עַת\rb* \rb what was troubling him|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and why|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |מַה־\rb*\rb |זֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Hathach|הֲתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb square|רְח֣וֹב\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb gate|שַֽׁעַר־\rb*, \v 7 \rb and Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had happened to him|קָרָ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb including|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the exact amount|פָּרָשַׁ֣ת\rb* \rb of money|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָן֙\rb* \rb had promised|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to pay|לִ֠שְׁקוֹל\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb treasury|גִּנְזֵ֥י\rb* \rb in order to destroy|לְאַבְּדָֽם׃\rb* \rb the Jews|בַּיְּהוּדִיִּים\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Mordecai also gave Hathach|נִתַּ֨ן\rb* \rb a copy|פַּתְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the written|כְּתָֽב־\rb* \rb decree|הַ֠דָּת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb issued|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb in Susa|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֤ן\rb* \rb for the destruction of the Jews|לְהַשְׁמִידָם֙\rb*, \rb to show|לְהַרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb and explain|וּלְהַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֖ר\rb*, \rb urging|וּלְצַוּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb her|עָלֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb to approach|לָב֨וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb*, \rb implore his favor|לְהִֽתְחַנֶּן־\rb*, \rb and plead|וּלְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb before him|מִלְּפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb her people|עַמָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So Hathach|הֲתָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb and relayed|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכָֽי׃\rb* \rb response|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb to Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb spoke|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Hathach|לַהֲתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and instructed him|וַתְּצַוֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb tell Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָֽי׃\rb*, \v 11 “\rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb officials|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb and the people|וְעַם־\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינ֨וֹת\rb* \rb know|יֽוֹדְעִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb law|דָּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb applies to every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or woman|וְאִשָּׁ֡ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb approaches|יָבֽוֹא־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֜ית\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֨ר\rb* \rb without|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb being summoned|יִקָּרֵ֗א\rb*— \rb that he be put to death|לְהָמִ֔ית\rb*. \rb Only if|לְ֠בַד\rb*\rb |מֵאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb extends|יֽוֹשִׁיט־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb scepter|שַׁרְבִ֥יט\rb* \rb may that person live|וְחָיָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb been summoned|נִקְרֵ֙אתי֙\rb* \rb to appear|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb for the past thirty|שְׁלוֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb When Esther’s|אֶסְתֵּֽר׃פ\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb were relayed|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb to Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכָ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*, \v 13 \rb he|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb sent back|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her|אֶסְתֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb this reply|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb*: “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb imagine that|תְּדַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb because you are|בְנַפְשֵׁ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּית־\rb* \rb you alone will escape|לְהִמָּלֵ֥ט\rb* \rb the fate of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you remain silent|הַחֲרֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |תַּחֲרִישִׁי֮\rb* \rb at this|הַזֹּאת֒\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb relief|רֶ֣וַח\rb* \rb and deliverance|וְהַצָּלָ֞ה\rb* \rb for the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb will arise|יַעֲמ֤וֹד\rb* \rb from another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb place|מִמָּק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַ֥תְּ\rb* \rb and your father’s|אָבִ֖יךְ\rb* \rb house|וּבֵית־\rb* \rb will perish|תֹּאבֵ֑דוּ\rb*. \rb And who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֔עַ\rb* \rb if perhaps|אִם־\rb* \rb you have come|הִגַּ֖עַתְּ\rb* \rb to the kingdom|לַמַּלְכֽוּת׃\rb* \rb for such a time|לְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb as this|כָּזֹ֔את\rb*?”
\p \v 15 \rb Then Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb sent|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb this reply|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָֽי׃\rb*: \v 16 “\rb Go|לֵךְ֩\rb* \rb and assemble|כְּנ֨וֹס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֜ים\rb* \rb who can be found|הַֽנִּמְצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb in Susa|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֗ן\rb*, \rb and fast|וְצ֣וּמוּ\rb* \rb for me|עָ֠לַי\rb*. \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb eat|תֹּאכְל֨וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or drink|תִּשְׁתּ֜וּ\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb*, \rb night|לַ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb or day|וָי֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb and my maidens|וְנַעֲרֹתַ֖י\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb will fast|אָצ֣וּם\rb* \rb as you do|כֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb After that|וּבְכֵ֞ן\rb*, \rb I will go|אָב֤וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb even though|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb it is against|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the law|כַדָּ֔ת\rb*. \rb And if|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I perish|אָבַ֖דְתִּי\rb*, \rb I perish|אָבָֽדְתִּי׃\rb*!\f + \fr 4:16 \ft Or \fqa if I am destroyed, then I will be destroyed!\f*”
\p \v 17 \rb So Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb* \rb went|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּֽר׃ס\rb* \rb had instructed|צִוְּתָ֥ה\rb* \rb him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 Esther Approaches the King
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb put on|וַתִּלְבַּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb her royal robes|מַלְכ֔וּת\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֞ד\rb* \rb in the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֔ית\rb* \rb court|בַּחֲצַ֤ר\rb* \rb of the palace|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb across from|נֹ֖כַח\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb quarters|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. \rb The king|וְ֠הַמֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֞ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his royal|מַלְכוּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֤א\rb* \rb in the royal|הַמַּלְכ֔וּת\rb* \rb courtroom|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb facing|נֹ֖כַח\rb* \rb the|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb As soon as the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|כִרְא֨וֹת\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֶ֙דֶת֙\rb* \rb in the court|בֶּֽחָצֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb she found|נָשְׂאָ֥ה\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in his sight|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb extended|וַיּ֨וֹשֶׁט\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb scepter|שַׁרְבִ֤יט\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb toward Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֗ר\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and she|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb approached|וַתִּקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb and touched|וַתִּגַּ֖ע\rb* \rb the tip|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of the scepter|הַשַּׁרְבִֽיט׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is it|לָּ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb*?” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb inquired|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb What is|וּמַה־\rb* \rb your request|בַּקָּשָׁתֵ֛ךְ\rb*? \rb Even up to|עַד־\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּלְכ֖וּת\rb*, \rb it will be given|וְיִנָּ֥תֵֽן\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*,”\rb |ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb may the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Haman|וְהָמָן֙\rb* \rb come|יָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have prepared|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb for the king|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 “\rb Hurry|מַהֲרוּ֙\rb*,” \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb and bring Haman|הָמָ֔ן\rb*, \rb so we can do|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb has requested|דְּבַ֣ר\rb*.”
\p \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and Haman|וְהָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb had prepared|עָשְׂתָ֥ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb And as they drank|בְּמִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb their wine|הַיַּ֔יִן\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּר֙\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is your petition|שְּׁאֵלָתֵ֖ךְ\rb*? \rb It will be given|וְיִנָּ֣תֵֽן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb What is|וּמַה־\rb* \rb your request|בַּקָּשָׁתֵ֛ךְ\rb*? \rb Even up to|עַד־\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּלְכ֖וּת\rb*, \rb it will be fulfilled|וְתֵעָֽשׂ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |וַתֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb replied|וַתַּ֥עַן\rb*, “\rb This is my petition|שְׁאֵלָתִ֖י\rb* \rb and my request|וּבַקָּשָׁתִֽי׃\rb*: \v 8 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֜ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb to grant|לָתֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my petition|שְׁאֵ֣לָתִ֔י\rb* \rb and fulfill|וְלַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my request|בַּקָּשָׁתִ֑י\rb*, \rb may the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Haman|וְהָמָ֗ן\rb* \rb come|יָב֧וֹא\rb* \rb tomorrow|וּמָחָ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I will prepare|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Then I will answer|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb question|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*.”
\s1 Haman’s Plot against Mordecai
\p \v 9 \rb That|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָן֙\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb full of joy|שָׂמֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb and glad|וְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb of heart|לֵ֑ב\rb*. \rb At the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate, however|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb he|הָמָ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb saw|וְכִרְאוֹת֩\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֜י\rb*, \rb who did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb rise|קָם֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb or tremble in fear|זָ֣ע\rb* \rb at his presence|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*. \rb And Haman|הָמָ֛ן\rb* \rb was filled|וַיִּמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with rage|חֵמָֽה׃\rb* \rb toward|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Nevertheless, Haman|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb restrained himself|וַיִּתְאַפַּ֣ק\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb And calling for|וַיִּשְׁלַ֛ח\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his friends|אֹהֲבָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Zeresh|זֶ֥רֶשׁ\rb*, \v 11 \rb Haman|הָמָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recounted|וַיְסַפֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb his glorious|כְּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb wealth|עָשְׁר֖וֹ\rb*, \rb his many|וְרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb all the ways|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had honored|גִּדְּל֤וֹ\rb* \rb and promoted him|נִשְּׂא֔וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the other officials|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb and servants|וְעַבְדֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb What is more|אַ֣ף\rb*,” \rb Haman|הָמָן֒\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*, “\rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb invited|הֵבִיאָה֩\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֑י\rb* \rb to join|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she prepared|עָשָׂ֖תָה\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am invited|קָֽרוּא־\rb* \rb back|וְגַם־\rb* \rb tomorrow|לְמָחָ֛ר\rb* \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Yet none|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb of this|זֶ֕ה\rb* \rb satisfies|שֹׁוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb* \rb as|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb long|עֵ֗ת\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֣י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִ֔י\rb* \rb sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb His wife|אִשְׁתּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb Zeresh|זֶ֨רֶשׁ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his friends|אֹֽהֲבָ֗יו\rb* \rb told|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֩\rb*, “\rb Have them build|יַֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb a gallows|עֵץ֮\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֒\rb* \rb high|גָּבֹ֣הַּ\rb*,\f + \fr 5:14 \fqa 50 cubits \ft is approximately 75 feet or 22.9 meters high.\f* \rb and ask|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the morning|וּבַבֹּ֣קֶר׀\rb* \rb to have Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַי֙\rb* \rb hanged|וְיִתְל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֔יו\rb*. \rb Then go|וּבֹֽא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and enjoy yourself|שָׂמֵ֑חַ\rb*.”
\p \rb The advice|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּיטַ֧ב\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֖ן\rb*, \rb and he had the gallows|הָעֵֽץ׃פ\rb* \rb constructed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 Mordecai Is Honored
\p \v 1 \rb That|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb sleep|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb escaped|נָדְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*; \rb so he ordered|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of Records|הַזִּכְרֹנוֹת֙\rb*, \rb the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 6:1 \ft Or \fqa the Book of Memorials, the Annals \ft or \fqa the Book of Records of Historical Events\f* \rb to be|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb brought in|לְהָבִ֞יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and read|נִקְרָאִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And there it was found|וַיִּמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb recorded|כָת֗וּב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֜י\rb* \rb had exposed|הִגִּ֨יד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Bigthana|בִּגְתָ֣נָא\rb*\f + \fr 6:2 \fqa Bigthana \ft is a variant of \fqa Bigthan\ft ; see Esther 2:21.\f* \rb and Teresh|וָתֶ֗רֶשׁ\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the eunuchs|סָרִיסֵ֣י\rb* \rb who guarded|מִשֹּׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb entrance|הַסַּ֑ף\rb*, \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they had conspired|בִּקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb to assassinate|לִשְׁלֹ֣חַ\rb*\rb |יָ֔ד\rb* \rb King|בַּמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb inquired|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb honor|יְקָ֧ר\rb* \rb or dignity|וּגְדוּלָּ֛ה\rb* \rb has been bestowed|נַּעֲשָׂ֞ה\rb* \rb on Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb this act|זֶ֑ה\rb*?”
\p “\rb Nothing|לֹא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb has been done|נַעֲשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb attendants|נַעֲרֵ֤י\rb*\rb |מְשָׁ֣רְתָ֔יו\rb*.
\p \v 4 “\rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb is in the court|בֶחָצֵ֑ר\rb*?” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb Now Haman|וְהָמָ֣ן\rb* \rb had just entered|בָּ֗א\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|לַחֲצַ֤ר\rb* \rb of the palace|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to ask|לֵאמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to hang|לִתְלוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|הָעֵ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had prepared|הֵכִ֥ין\rb* \rb for him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb attendants|נַעֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb answered him|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb*, “\rb Haman|הָמָ֖ן\rb* \rb is there|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb standing|עֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb in the court|בֶּחָצֵ֑ר\rb*.”
\p “\rb Bring him in|יָבֽוֹא׃\rb*,” \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Haman|הָמָן֒\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבוֹא֮\rb*, \rb and the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb should be done|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb for the man|בָּאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb is delighted|חָפֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb to honor|בִּיקָר֑וֹ\rb*?”
\p \rb Now Haman|הָמָן֙\rb* \rb thought|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to himself|בְּלִבּ֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Whom|לְמִ֞י\rb* \rb would the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb be delighted|יַחְפֹּ֥ץ\rb* \rb to honor|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יְקָ֖ר\rb* \rb more|יוֹתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb than me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 7 \rb And Haman|הָמָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb For the man|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb is delighted|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb to honor|בִּיקָרֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb have them bring|יָבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb* \rb a royal|מַלְכ֔וּת\rb* \rb robe|לְב֣וּשׁ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king himself|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb has worn|לָֽבַשׁ־\rb* \rb and a horse|וְס֗וּס\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king himself|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb has ridden|רָכַ֤ב\rb*— \rb one with|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb a royal|מַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb crest|כֶּ֥תֶר\rb* \rb placed|נִתַּ֛ן\rb* \rb on its head|בְּרֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Let|וְנָת֨וֹן\rb* \rb the robe|הַלְּב֜וּשׁ\rb* \rb and the horse|וְהַסּ֗וּס\rb* \rb be entrusted|עַל־\rb*\rb |יַד־\rb* \rb to one|אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb most noble|הַֽפַּרְתְּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb princes|מִשָּׂרֵ֤י\rb*. \rb Let them array|וְהִלְבִּ֙ישׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb wants|חָפֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb to honor|בִּֽיקָר֑וֹ\rb* \rb and parade him|וְהִרְכִּיבֻ֤הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horse|הַסּוּס֙\rb* \rb through the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb square|בִּרְח֣וֹב\rb*, \rb proclaiming|וְקָרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כָּ֚כָה\rb* \rb is done|יֵעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb is delighted|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb to honor|בִּיקָרֽוֹ׃\rb*!’”
\p \v 10 “\rb Hurry|מַ֠הֵר\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Haman|לְהָמָ֗ן\rb*, “\rb and do|וַֽעֲשֵׂה־\rb*\rb |כֵן֙\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you proposed|דִּבַּ֔רְתָּ\rb*. \rb Take|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|הַלְּב֤וּשׁ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the horse|הַסּוּס֙\rb* \rb to Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכַ֣י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb who is sitting|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb neglect|תַּפֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have suggested|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb So Haman|הָמָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the robe|הַלְּב֣וּשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the horse|הַסּ֔וּס\rb*, \rb arrayed|וַיַּלְבֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb*, \rb and paraded him|וַיַּרְכִּיבֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb through the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb square|בִּרְח֣וֹב\rb*, \rb crying out|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb This is what|כָּ֚כָה\rb* \rb is done|יֵעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb is delighted|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb to honor|בִּיקָרֽוֹ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 12 \rb Then Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb But Haman|וְהָמָן֙\rb* \rb rushed|נִדְחַ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb with his head|רֹֽאשׁ׃\rb* \rb covered|וַחֲפ֥וּי\rb* \rb in grief|אָבֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Haman|הָמָ֜ן\rb* \rb told|וַיְסַפֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb Zeresh|לְזֶ֤רֶשׁ\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his friends|אֹ֣הֲבָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had happened|קָרָ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb His advisers|חֲכָמָ֜יו\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Zeresh|וְזֶ֣רֶשׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֩אמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb to him|ל֨וֹ\rb*, “\rb Since|אִ֣ם\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֞י\rb*, \rb before|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb your downfall|לִנְפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb has begun|הַחִלּ֨וֹתָ\rb*, \rb is Jewish|הַיְּהוּדִ֡ים\rb*,\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb you will not prevail|תוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb against him|ל֔וֹ\rb* — \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb surely you will fall|נָפ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |תִּפּ֖וֹל\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb While they were still|עוֹדָם֙\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבְּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb with Haman|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb eunuchs|וְסָרִיסֵ֥י\rb* \rb arrived|הִגִּ֑יעוּ\rb* \rb and rushed|וַיַּבְהִ֙לוּ֙\rb*\rb |לְהָבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb had prepared|עָשְׂתָ֥ה\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 Esther Pleads for Her People
\p \v 1 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and Haman|וְהָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to dine|לִשְׁתּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb the queen|הַמַּלְכָּֽה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and as they drank|בְּמִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb their wine|הַיַּ֔יִן\rb* \rb on that second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb once more|גַּ֣ם\rb*\rb |לְאֶסְתֵּ֜ר\rb*, “\rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֥ר\rb*, \rb what is|מַה־\rb* \rb your petition|שְּׁאֵלָתֵ֛ךְ\rb*? \rb It will be given|וְתִנָּ֣תֵֽן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb What is|וּמַה־\rb* \rb your request|בַּקָּשָׁתֵ֛ךְ\rb*? \rb Even up to|עַד־\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּלְכ֖וּת\rb*, \rb it will be fulfilled|וְתֵעָֽשׂ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּה֙\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb replied|וַתַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb grant|תִּנָּֽתֶן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֤י\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb as my petition|בִּשְׁאֵ֣לָתִ֔י\rb*, \rb and the lives of my people|וְעַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb as my request|בְּבַקָּשָׁתִֽי׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb my people|וְעַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have been sold out|נִמְכַּ֙רְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to destruction|לְהַשְׁמִ֖יד\rb*, \rb death|לַהֲר֣וֹג\rb*, \rb and annihilation|וּלְאַבֵּ֑ד\rb*. \rb If|וְ֠אִלּוּ\rb* \rb we had merely been sold|נִמְכַּ֙רְנוּ֙\rb* \rb as menservants|לַעֲבָדִ֨ים\rb* \rb and maidservants|וְלִשְׁפָח֤וֹת\rb*, \rb I would have remained silent|הֶחֱרַ֔שְׁתִּי\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb such distress|הַצָּ֛ר\rb* \rb would justify|שֹׁוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb burdening|בְּנֵ֥זֶק\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb spoke up|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb is this|זֶה֙\rb*, \rb and where|וְאֵֽי־\rb*\rb |זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the one|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb would|מְלָא֥וֹ\rb*\rb |לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb devise|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 7:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa whose heart has filled him to do\f* \rb such a scheme?|כֵּֽן׃\rb*”
\p \v 6 \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר־\rb*, “\rb The adversary|צַ֣ר\rb* \rb and enemy|וְאוֹיֵ֔ב\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb wicked man|הָרָ֖ע\rb* — \rb Haman|הָמָ֥ן\rb*!”
\p \rb And Haman|וְהָמָ֣ן\rb* \rb stood in terror|נִבְעַ֔ת\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and queen|וְהַמַּלְכָּֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Hanging of Haman
\p \v 7 \rb In his fury|בַּחֲמָתוֹ֙\rb*, \rb the king|וְהַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb arose|קָ֤ם\rb* \rb from drinking|מִמִּשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb his wine|הַיַּ֔יִן\rb* \rb and went to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבִּיתָ֑ן\rb* \rb garden|גִּנַּ֖ת\rb*, \rb while Haman|וְהָמָ֣ן\rb* \rb stayed behind|עָמַ֗ד\rb* \rb to beg|לְבַקֵּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb Esther|מֵֽאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he realized|רָאָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb was planning|כָלְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a terrible fate|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb for him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Just as the king|וְהַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb returned|שָׁב֩\rb* \rb from the palace|הַבִּיתָ֜ן\rb* \rb garden|מִגִּנַּ֨ת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the banquet hall|בֵּ֣ית׀\rb*\rb |מִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַיַּ֗יִן\rb*, \rb Haman|וְהָמָן֙\rb* \rb was falling|נֹפֵ֔ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the couch|הַמִּטָּה֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb was reclining|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb exclaimed|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Would he actually|הֲ֠גַם\rb* \rb assault|לִכְבּ֧וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֛ה\rb* \rb while|עִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb I am in the palace|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb*?”
\p \rb As soon as the words|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb had left|יָצָא֙\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb mouth|מִפִּ֣י\rb*, \rb they covered|חָפֽוּ׃ס\rb* \rb Haman’s|הָמָ֖ן\rb* \rb face|וּפְנֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Harbonah|חַ֠רְבוֹנָה\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the eunuchs|הַסָּרִיסִ֜ים\rb* \rb attending|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*: “\rb There|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb is a gallows|הָעֵ֣ץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb high|גָּבֹ֖הַּ\rb*\f + \fr 7:9 \fqa 50 cubits \ft is approximately 75 feet or 22.9 meters high.\f* \rb at Haman’s|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*. \rb He|הָמָ֟ן\rb* \rb had it built|עָשָׂ֪ה\rb* \rb for Mordecai|לְֽמָרְדֳּכַ֞י\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb gave the report|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb that saved|ט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עֹמֵד֙\rb*.”
\p “\rb Hang him|תְּלֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb on it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*!” \rb declared|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So they hanged|וַיִּתְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|הָעֵ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had prepared|הֵכִ֣ין\rb* \rb for Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb*. \rb Then the fury|וַחֲמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb subsided|שָׁכָֽכָה׃פ\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 Esther Appeals for the Jews
\p \v 1 \rb That same|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb awarded|נָתַ֞ן\rb* \rb Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb the estate|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Haman|הָמָ֖ן\rb*, \rb the enemy|צֹרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִיִּים\rb*. \rb And Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֗י\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |מַ֥ה\rb* \rb had revealed|הִגִּ֥ידָה\rb* \rb his relation|הוּא־\rb* \rb to her|לָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֨סַר\rb* \rb the signet ring|טַבַּעְתּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he had recovered|הֶֽעֱבִיר֙\rb* \rb from Haman|מֵֽהָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb and presented it|וַֽיִּתְּנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to Mordecai|לְמָרְדֳּכָ֑י\rb*. \rb And Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb appointed|וַתָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the estate|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Haman|הָמָֽן׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And once again|וַתּ֣וֹסֶף\rb*, \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֗ר\rb* \rb addressed|וַתְּדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*. \rb She fell|וַתִּפֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb at|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֑יו\rb* \rb weeping|וַתֵּ֣בְךְּ\rb* \rb and begged|וַתִּתְחַנֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb to revoke|לְהַֽעֲבִיר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the evil|רָעַת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb scheme|מַֽחֲשַׁבְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of Haman|הָמָ֣ן\rb* \rb the Agagite|הָֽאֲגָגִ֔י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had devised|חָשַׁ֖ב\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb extended|וַיּ֤וֹשֶׁט\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֑ב\rb* \rb scepter|שַׁרְבִ֣ט\rb* \rb toward Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb*,\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and she|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb arose|וַתָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|עַל־\rb*\rb |ט֜וֹב\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb*,” \rb she said|וַ֠תֹּאמֶר\rb*, “\rb and if I have found|מָצָ֧אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֣ן\rb* \rb in his sight|לְפָנָ֗יו\rb*, \rb and the matter|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb seems proper|וְכָשֵׁ֤ר\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am pleasing|וְטוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb in his sight|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*, \rb may an order be written|יִכָּתֵ֞ב\rb* \rb to revoke|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the letters|הַסְּפָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb that the scheming|מַחֲשֶׁ֜בֶת\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֤ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Hammedatha|הַמְּדָ֙תָא֙\rb*, \rb the Agagite|הָאֲגָגִ֔י\rb*, \rb wrote|כָּתַ֗ב\rb* \rb to destroy|לְאַבֵּד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינ֥וֹת\rb*. \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb how|אֵיכָכָ֤ה\rb* \rb could I bear|אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb to see|וְֽרָאִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb the disaster|בָּרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb would befall|יִמְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*? \rb How|וְאֵֽיכָכָ֤ה\rb* \rb could I bear|אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb to see|וְֽרָאִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb the destruction|בְּאָבְדַ֖ן\rb* \rb of my kindred|מוֹלַדְתִּֽי׃ס\rb*?”
\s1 The Decree of Xerxes
\p \v 7 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb the Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and Mordecai|וּֽלְמָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִ֑י\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I have given|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb Haman’s|הָמָ֜ן\rb* \rb estate|בֵית־\rb* \rb to Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֗ר\rb*,\rb |וְאֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and he was hanged|תָּל֣וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb because|עַ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he attacked|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb the Jews|בַּיְּהוּדִיִּים׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Now you|וְ֠אַתֶּם\rb* \rb may write|כִּתְב֨וּ\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb as|כַּטּ֤וֹב\rb* \rb you please|בְּעֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb regarding|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֜ים\rb*, \rb and seal it|וְחִתְמ֖וּ\rb* \rb with the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb signet ring|בְּטַבַּ֣עַת\rb*. \rb For a decree|כְתָ֞ב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is written|נִכְתָּ֣ב\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and sealed|וְנַחְתּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb with the royal|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb signet ring|בְּטַבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb cannot|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb be revoked|לְהָשִֽׁיב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb At once|בָּֽעֵת־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb scribes|סֹפְרֵֽי־\rb* \rb were summoned|וַיִּקָּרְא֣וּ\rb*, \rb and on the twenty-third day|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֮\rb* \rb of the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֜י\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb* (\rb |הַ֠הִיא\rb* \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Sivan|סִיוָ֗ן\rb*\f + \fr 8:9 \fqa Sivan \ft is the third month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of May and June.\f*), \rb they recorded|וַיִּכָּתֵ֣ב\rb* \rb all of|כְּֽכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכַ֣י\rb* \rb orders|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֡ים\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶ֣ל\rb* \rb the satraps|הָאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנִֽים־\rb*, \rb governors|וְהַפַּחוֹת֩\rb*, \rb and princes|וְשָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the 127|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּמֵאָה֙\rb* \rb provinces|הַמְּדִינ֜וֹת\rb* \rb from India|מֵהֹ֣דּוּ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Cush|כּ֗וּשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 8:9 \ft That is, to the upper Nile region\f* — \rb writing to each province|מְדִינָ֔ה\rb*\rb |מְדִינָ֤ה\rb* \rb in its own script|וּמְדִינָה֙\rb*,\rb |כִּכְתָבָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb to every people|וָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in their own language|כִּלְשֹׁנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and to|וְאֶ֨ל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb in their own script|כִּכְתָבָ֖ם\rb* \rb and language|וְכִלְשׁוֹנָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Mordecai wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֗ב\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵרֹ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and sealed it|וַיַּחְתֹּ֖ם\rb* \rb with the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb signet ring|בְּטַבַּ֣עַת\rb*. \rb He sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb the documents|סְפָרִ֡ים\rb* \rb by|בְּיַד֩\rb* \rb mounted|בַּסּוּסִ֜ים\rb* \rb couriers|הָרָצִ֨ים\rb* \rb riding on|רֹכְבֵ֤י\rb* \rb swift horses|הָרֶ֙כֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb bred|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb from the royal|הָֽאֲחַשְׁתְּרָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb mares|הָֽרַמָּכִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb By these letters|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb permitted|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in each|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb and every city|עִיר־\rb*\rb |וָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb the right to assemble|לְהִקָּהֵל֮\rb* \rb and defend|עַל־\rb*\rb |וְלַעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb themselves|נַפְשָׁם֒\rb*, \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִיד֩\rb*, \rb kill|וְלַהֲרֹ֨ג\rb*, \rb and annihilate|וּלְאַבֵּ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the forces|חֵ֨יל\rb* \rb of any people|עַ֧ם\rb* \rb or province|וּמְדִינָ֛ה\rb* \rb hostile to them|הַצָּרִ֥ים\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb including women|וְנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb and children|טַ֣ף\rb*, \rb and to plunder|וּשְׁלָלָ֖ם\rb* \rb their possessions|לָבֽוֹז׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb day appointed|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb throughout all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the provinces|מְדִינ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb was the thirteenth|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb day of the twelfth|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb month|לְחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָֽר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 8:12 \fqa Adar \ft is the twelfth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of February and March.\f*
\p \v 13 \rb A copy|פַּתְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the text|הַכְּתָ֗ב\rb* \rb of the edict|דָּת֙\rb* \rb was to be issued|לְהִנָּ֤תֵֽן\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb and published|גָּל֖וּי\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעַמִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb so that the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִיִּים\rb* \rb would be|וְלִהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb ready|עֲתוּדִים\rb* \rb on that|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|לַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb to avenge themselves|לְהִנָּקֵ֖ם\rb* \rb on their enemies|מֵאֹיְבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb The couriers|הָרָצִ֞ים\rb* \rb rode|רֹכְבֵ֤י\rb* \rb out|יָֽצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb in haste|מְבֹהָלִ֥ים\rb* \rb on their royal|הָֽאֲחַשְׁתְּרָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb horses|הָרֶ֙כֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb pressed on|וּדְחוּפִ֖ים\rb* \rb by the command|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb And the edict|וְהַדָּ֥ת\rb* \rb was also issued|נִתְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֥ן\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֞י\rb* \rb went out|יָצָ֣א׀\rb* \rb from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in royal garments|בִּלְב֤וּשׁ\rb*\rb |מַלְכוּת֙\rb* \rb of blue|תְּכֵ֣לֶת\rb* \rb and white|וָח֔וּר\rb*, \rb with a large|גְּדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb crown|וַעֲטֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb and a purple|וְאַרְגָּמָ֑ן\rb* \rb robe|וְתַכְרִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb of fine linen|בּ֖וּץ\rb*. \rb And the city|וְהָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Susa|שׁוּשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb shouted|צָהֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and rejoiced|וְשָׂמֵֽחָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb For the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִ֕ים\rb* \rb it was a time of|הָֽיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb light|אוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and gladness|וְשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb*, \rb of joy|וְשָׂשֹׂ֖ן\rb* \rb and honor|וִיקָֽר׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb In every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינָ֨ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֜ה\rb* \rb and every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb*\rb |וָעִ֗יר\rb*, \rb wherever|מְקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb edict|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb and decree|וְדָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb reached|מַגִּ֔יעַ\rb*, \rb there was joy|שִׂמְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb and gladness|וְשָׂשׂוֹן֙\rb* \rb among the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb with feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and celebrating|וְי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |ט֑וֹב\rb*. \rb And many|וְרַבִּ֞ים\rb* \rb of the people|מֵֽעַמֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb themselves became Jews|מִֽתְיַהֲדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the fear|פַּֽחַד־\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 The Jews Destroy Their Enemies
\p \v 1 \rb On the thirteenth|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |הִגִּ֧יעַ\rb* \rb of the twelfth|וּבִשְׁנֵים֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb month|חֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֗ר\rb*,\f + \fr 9:1 \fqa Adar \ft is the twelfth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of February and March; also in verses 15, 17, 19, and 21.\f* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb and edict|וְדָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb were to be executed|לְהֵעָשׂ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb On this day|בַּיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the enemies|אֹיְבֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb had hoped|שִׂבְּר֜וּ\rb* \rb to overpower|לִשְׁל֣וֹט\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb but their plan was overturned|וְנַהֲפ֣וֹךְ\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֛ים\rb* \rb overpowered|יִשְׁלְט֧וּ\rb* \rb those|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb who hated them|בְּשֹׂנְאֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb In each|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of the provinces|מְדִינוֹת֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֳחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֜ים\rb* \rb assembled|נִקְהֲל֨וּ\rb* \rb in their cities|בְּעָרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to attack|לִשְׁלֹ֣חַ\rb*\rb |יָ֔ד\rb* \rb those who sought|בִּמְבַקְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb to harm them|רָֽעָתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb could withstand|עָמַ֣ד\rb* \rb them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the fear of them|פַּחְדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb peoples|הָעַמִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the provinces|הַמְּדִינ֜וֹת\rb*, \rb the satraps|וְהָאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the governors|וְהַפַּח֗וֹת\rb*, \rb and the king’s|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb administrators|וְעֹשֵׂ֤י\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb helped|מְנַשְּׂאִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the fear|פַּֽחַד־\rb* \rb of Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַי֙\rb* \rb exercised great|גָ֤דוֹל\rb* \rb power in the palace|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and his fame|וְשָׁמְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb spread|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the provinces|הַמְּדִינ֑וֹת\rb* \rb as|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb he|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb became|הוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb more and more powerful|וְגָדֽוֹל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb The Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb put|וַיַּכּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |מַכַּת־\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹ֣יְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb killing|וְהֶ֖רֶג\rb* \rb and destroying them|וְאַבְדָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and they did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb as they pleased|כִּרְצוֹנָֽם׃\rb* \rb to those who hated them|בְשֹׂנְאֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 6 \rb In the citadel|הַבִּירָ֗ה\rb* \rb of Susa|וּבְשׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb*, \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb killed|הָרְג֤וּ\rb* \rb and destroyed|וְאַבֵּ֔ד\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb |וְאֵ֧ת׀\rb* \rb including Parshandatha|פַּרְשַׁנְדָּ֛תָא\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb Dalphon|דַּֽלְפ֖וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb Aspatha|אַסְפָּֽתָא׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb |וְאֵ֧ת׀\rb* \rb Poratha|פּוֹרָ֛תָא\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb Adalia|אֲדַלְיָ֖א\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb Aridatha|אֲרִידָֽתָא׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb |וְאֵ֤ת׀\rb* \rb Parmashta|פַּרְמַ֙שְׁתָּא֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb Arisai|אֲרִיסַ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb Aridai|אֲרִדַ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ת׀\rb* \rb and Vaizatha|וַיְזָֽתָא׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb They killed|הָרָ֑גוּ\rb* \rb these ten|עֲ֠שֶׂרֶת\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Haman|הָמָ֧ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Hammedatha|הַמְּדָ֛תָא\rb*, \rb the enemy|צֹרֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֖ים\rb*, \rb but they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lay|שָׁלְח֖וּ\rb* \rb a hand|יָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb on the plunder|וּבַ֨בִּזָּ֔ה\rb*.
\s1 Haman’s Sons Hanged
\p \v 11 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb*\rb |בָּ֣א\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the number|מִסְפַּ֧ר\rb* \rb of those killed|הַֽהֲרוּגִ֛ים\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָ֖ה\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֥ן\rb* \rb was reported to|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*, \v 12 \rb who|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Esther|לְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb*, “\rb In the citadel|הַבִּירָ֡ה\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֨ים\rb* \rb have killed|הָרְגוּ֩\rb* \rb and destroyed|וְאַבֵּ֜ד\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֗ישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb including Haman’s|הָמָ֔ן\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*. \rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have they done|עָשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb in the rest|בִּשְׁאָ֛ר\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינ֥וֹת\rb*? \rb Now what is|וּמַה־\rb* \rb your petition|שְּׁאֵֽלָתֵךְ֙\rb*? \rb It will be given|וְיִנָּ֣תֵֽן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb And what|וּמַה־\rb* \rb further|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb do you request|בַּקָּשָׁתֵ֥ךְ\rb*? \rb It will be fulfilled|וְתֵעָֽשׂ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּר֙\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|עַל־\rb*\rb |ט֔וֹב\rb*\rb |יִנָּתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb may the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Susa|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb have tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb to carry out|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb today’s|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb edict|כְּדָ֣ת\rb*, \rb and may the bodies of Haman’s|הָמָ֖ן\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb be hanged|יִתְל֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|הָעֵֽץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb that this|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb be done|לְהֵֽעָשׂ֣וֹת\rb*. \rb An edict|דָּ֖ת\rb* \rb was issued|וַתִּנָּתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in Susa|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֑ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and they hanged|תָּלֽוּ׃\rb* \rb the ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Haman|הָמָ֖ן\rb*. \v 15 \rb On the fourteenth|אַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the month|לְחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֔ר\rb*, \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִיִּים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Susa|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֗ן\rb* \rb came together|וַיִּֽקָּהֲל֞וּ\rb* \rb again|גַּ֠ם\rb* \rb and put to death|וַיַּֽהַרְג֣וּ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb there|בְשׁוּשָׁ֔ן\rb*, \rb but they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lay|שָׁלְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a hand|יָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb on the plunder|וּבַ֨בִּזָּ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb The rest|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֡ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb in the royal|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb provinces|בִּמְדִינ֨וֹת\rb* \rb also assembled|נִקְהֲל֣וּ׀\rb* \rb to defend|וְעָמֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb themselves|נַפְשָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb and rid themselves|וְנ֙וֹחַ֙\rb* \rb of their enemies|מֵאֹ֣יְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb They killed|וְהָרֹג֙\rb* \rb 75,000|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb who hated them|בְּשֹׂ֣נְאֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb but they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lay|שָֽׁלְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a hand|יָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb on the plunder|וּבַ֨בִּזָּ֔ה\rb*. \v 17 \rb This was done on the thirteenth|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day|בְּיוֹם־\rb* \rb of the month|לְחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and on the fourteenth day|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb they rested|וְנ֗וֹחַ\rb*, \rb making it|וְעָשֹׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb a day|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb of feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and joy|וְשִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Feast of Purim Instituted
\p \v 18 \rb The Jews|וְהַיְּהוּדִיִּים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Susa, however|בְּשׁוּשָׁ֗ן\rb*, \rb had assembled|נִקְהֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb on the thirteenth|בִּשְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb and the fourteenth|וּבְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb days of the month|עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*. \rb So they rested|וְנ֗וֹחַ\rb* \rb on the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb day|עָשָׂר֙\rb*, \rb making|וְעָשֹׂ֣ה\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb a day|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb of feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and joy|וְשִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb This is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb the rural|הַפְּרוֹזִים\rb* \rb Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֣ים\rb*, \rb who live|הַיֹּשְׁבִים֮\rb* \rb in the villages|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַפְּרָזוֹת֒\rb*, \rb observe|עֹשִׂ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb* \rb the fourteenth day|אַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb of the month|לְחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֔ר\rb* \rb as a day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of joy|שִׂמְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb and feasting|וּמִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb*. \rb It is a holiday|וְי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb for sending|וּמִשְׁל֥וֹחַ\rb* \rb gifts|מָנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another|לְרֵעֵֽהוּ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recorded|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb events|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the provinces|מְדִינוֹת֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb both near|הַקְּרוֹבִ֖ים\rb* \rb and far|וְהָרְחוֹקִֽים׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb to establish|לְקַיֵּם֮\rb* \rb among them|עֲלֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb an annual|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְשָׁנָֽה׃\rb*\rb |לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb celebration|עֹשִׂ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|אַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb and fifteenth|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb days|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the month|לְחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb*\rb |יוֹם־\rb* \v 22 \rb as the days|כַּיָּמִ֗ים\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb gained rest|נָ֨חוּ\rb* \rb from their enemies|מֵא֣וֹיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and the month|וְהַחֹ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb their sorrow|מִיָּגוֹן֙\rb* \rb turned|נֶהְפַּ֨ךְ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to joy|לְשִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb and their mourning|וּמֵאֵ֖בֶל\rb* \rb into a holiday|לְי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |ט֑וֹב\rb*. \rb He wrote that these were to be|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb days|יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb of feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb and joy|וְשִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb of sending|וּמִשְׁל֤וֹחַ\rb* \rb gifts|מָנוֹת֙\rb* \rb to one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|לְרֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and|וּמַתָּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the poor|לָֽאֶבְיוֹנִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb agreed to continue|וְקִבֵּל֙\rb* \rb the custom|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had started|הֵחֵ֖לּוּ\rb*, \rb as|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֖י\rb* \rb had written|כָּתַ֥ב\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb Haman|הָמָ֨ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Hammedatha|הַמְּדָ֜תָא\rb*, \rb the Agagite|הָֽאֲגָגִ֗י\rb*, \rb the enemy|צֹרֵר֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb had plotted|חָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb to destroy them|לְאַבְּדָ֑ם\rb* \rb and had cast|וְהִפִּ֥יל\rb* \rb the Pur|פּוּר֙\rb* \rb (that is|ה֣וּא\rb*, \rb the lot|הַגּוֹרָ֔ל\rb*) \rb to crush|לְהֻמָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and destroy them|וּֽלְאַבְּדָֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb But when it came|וּבְבֹאָהּ֮\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb*, \rb he commanded|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb by|עִם־\rb* \rb letter|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that the wicked|הָרָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb scheme|מַחֲשַׁבְתּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Haman had devised|חָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb should come back|יָשׁ֞וּב\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his own head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and that he|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb should be hanged|וְתָל֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the gallows|הָעֵֽץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb days|לַיָּמִ֨ים\rb* \rb are called|קָֽרְאוּ֩\rb* \rb Purim|פוּרִים֙\rb*, \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb the word|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb Pur|הַפּ֔וּר\rb*.
\p \rb Because of|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֕ן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the instructions|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb letter|הָאִגֶּ֣רֶת\rb*, \rb and because of all|וּמָֽה־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כָּ֔כָה\rb* \rb they had seen|רָא֣וּ\rb* \rb and experienced|וּמָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הִגִּ֖יעַ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֩׀\rb* \rb bound themselves|וְקִבֵּל\rb* \rb to establish the custom|קִיְּמ֣וּ\rb* \rb that they|עֲלֵיהֶ֨ם׀\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and their descendants|זַרְעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְעַ֨ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who join|הַנִּלְוִ֤ים\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb should not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb fail|יַעֲב֔וֹר\rb*\rb |לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb to celebrate|עֹשִׂ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִים֙\rb* \rb at the appointed time|וְכִזְמַנָּ֑ם\rb* \rb each|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb and every year|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְשָׁנָֽה׃\rb*, \rb according to their regulation|כִּכְתָבָ֖ם\rb*. \v 28 \rb These|הָ֠אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb days|וְהַיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb should be remembered|נִזְכָּרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and celebrated|וְנַעֲשִׂ֜ים\rb* \rb by every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |וָד֗וֹר\rb*, \rb family|מִשְׁפָּחָה֙\rb*\rb |וּמִשְׁפָּחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb province|מְדִינָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמְדִינָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and city|וְעִ֣יר\rb*\rb |וָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb so that these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb days|וִימֵ֞י\rb* \rb of Purim|הַפּוּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb should not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb fail to be observed|יַֽעַבְרוּ֙\rb* \rb among|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb nor should the memory of them|וְזִכְרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb fade|יָס֥וּף\rb* \rb from their descendants|מִזַּרְעָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb So Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Esther|אֶסְתֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Abihail|אֲבִיחַ֛יִל\rb*, \rb along with Mordecai|וּמָרְדֳּכַ֥י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִ֖י\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wrote|וַ֠תִּכְתֹּב\rb* \rb with full|כָּל־\rb* \rb authority|תֹּ֑קֶף\rb* \rb to confirm|לְקַיֵּ֗ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb second|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb letter|אִגֶּ֧רֶת\rb* \rb concerning Purim|הַפּוּרִ֛ים\rb*. \v 30 \rb And Mordecai sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb with words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb and truth|וֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the 127|שֶׁ֨בַע\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּמֵאָה֙\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb of the kingdom|מַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֑וֹשׁ\rb*, \v 31 \rb in order to confirm|לְקַיֵּ֡ם\rb*\rb |אֵת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb days|יְמֵי֩\rb* \rb of Purim|הַפֻּרִ֨ים\rb* \rb at their appointed time|בִּזְמַנֵּיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֤י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִי֙\rb* \rb and Queen|הַמַּלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb Esther|וְאֶסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb had established them|קִיַּ֨ם\rb* \rb and|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb had committed|קִיְּמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb themselves|נַפְשָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and their descendants|זַרְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb to the times|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of fasting|הַצֹּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and lamentation|וְזַעֲקָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb So Esther’s|אֶסְתֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb decree|וּמַאֲמַ֣ר\rb* \rb confirmed|קִיַּ֕ם\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb regulations|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb about Purim|הַפֻּרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb which were written|וְנִכְתָּ֖ב\rb* \rb into the record|בַּסֵּֽפֶר׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Tribute to Xerxes and Mordecai
\p \v 1 \rb Now King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחָשֵׁרֹשׁ\rb* \rb imposed|וַיָּשֶׂם֩\rb* \rb tribute|מַ֛ס\rb* \rb throughout|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb even to its farthest shores|וְאִיֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of Mordecai’s|מָרְדֳּכַ֔י\rb* \rb powerful|תָקְפּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and magnificent|וּגְב֣וּרָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb accomplishments|מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb*, \rb together with the full account|וּפָרָשַׁת֙\rb* \rb of the greatness|גְּדֻלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb had raised him|גִּדְּל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Media|מָדַ֥י\rb* \rb and Persia|וּפָרָֽס׃\rb*? \v 3 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb Mordecai|מָרְדֳּכַ֣י\rb* \rb the Jew|הַיְּהוּדִ֗י\rb* \rb was second|מִשְׁנֶה֙\rb* \rb only to King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb preeminent|וְגָדוֹל֙\rb* \rb among the Jews|לַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and highly favored|וְרָצ֖וּי\rb* \rb by his many|לְרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb kinsmen|אֶחָ֑יו\rb*, \rb seeking|דֹּרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the good|טוֹב֙\rb* \rb of his people|לְעַמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and speaking|וְדֹבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his countrymen|זַרְעֽוֹ׃\rb*.
